  "description": "Active non-default CUDA 13 vLLM pooling fallback for BAAI bge-base-en-v1.5, a public MIT-licensed English embedding model for semantic search, RAG retrieval, clustering, and medium-cost passage ranking. The current TEI CUDA 1.9.3 profile remains the primary latest route and has retained B200, H200, L40S, and RTX6000 support, but B300/SM103 is disabled there after the pinned TEI runtime failed before readiness and sibling TEI diagnostics logged `cuda compute cap 103 is not supported`. This fallback reuses the already mirrored official vLLM 0.22.0 CUDA 13 image digest sha256:0fec7ec5f3e6bc168e54899935fb0557da908a4832a1dbc88e2debcf2f889416, moving the route off vLLM 0.21.0 because GHSA-94f4-hr76-p5j6 / CVE-2026-48746 affects OpenAI-compatible vLLM API exposure in >=v0.3.0,<v0.22.0. It launches with `--runner pooling` and selects CLS pooling with `use_activation=true` to match the upstream sentence-transformers Pooling plus Normalize modules. Hugging Face metadata refreshed on 2026-06-02T00Z reports private=false, gated=false, disabled=false, library_name=sentence-transformers, pipeline_tag=feature-extraction, license=mit, revision a5beb1e3e68b9ab74eb54cfd186867f64f240e1a, tags text-embeddings-inference/endpoints_compatible, and safetensors parameters I64=512 plus F32=109,482,240. The 2026-06-03T11Z TEI/vLLM parity pass compared 10 general retrieval/control texts between TEI on L40S and this vLLM profile on B300 with min cosine 0.9999883025, max unit-vector delta 0.0007503663, max norm delta 0.0000000357, and 768 dimensions throughout. The same cycle's persisted B300 matrix probe passed with 3 warmups and 10 measured /v1/embeddings requests: 54.034 s startup, 75 ms client-wall p50, 76 ms p95, 360.0 tokens/s, 1.13 GB VRAM, and HTTP 200. Keep default_eligible=false and is_latest=false because this vLLM runtime is only the B300 fallback; do not enable non-B300 cells until each has its own matrix evidence.",
